module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.LocallyBijective

/-!
# Bijectivity on a covering family of objects makes a morphism of sheaves of modules invertible

Let `(C, J)` be a site, let `R` be a sheaf of rings on it and let `f : M ⟶ N` be a morphism of
sheaves of `R`-modules. If `f` is **bijective on the sections over the objects of a family which
generates a covering sieve of every object**, then `f` is locally injective and locally
surjective, hence an isomorphism by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_isLocallyBijective`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_val_of_injective_on`: injectivity on the sections
  over the objects of a sieve-generating family makes a morphism of sheaves of modules locally
  injective.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallySurjective_val_of_surjective_on`: the surjective half.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_bijective_val_app_on`: **bijectivity on the sections over the
  objects of a sieve-generating family makes a morphism of sheaves of modules an isomorphism.**
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isoOfBijectiveValAppOn`: that isomorphism as data.

## Implementation notes

The two local properties are proved by enlarging a covering sieve, not by refining it: the
equalizer sieve of two sections identified by `f` contains every arrow out of an object of the
family on which `f` is injective, because the sections agree there, and a sieve is downward
closed, so it contains the whole generated sieve; the image sieve of a section contains every
such arrow for the same reason.  `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.superset_covering` then
concludes.  No sheaf condition on `M` or `N` is used for either local property — only for the
passage from local bijectivity to invertibility, which is where
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_isLocallyBijective` uses that both are sheaves.

The hypotheses are stated on `f.val.app (op Z)`, the map on the sections over `Z`; local
injectivity and local surjectivity of a morphism of sheaves of modules are by definition those of
the underlying morphism of presheaves of abelian groups, whose components have the same
underlying functions.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Section 03CX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03CX)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

universe v v' u u'

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}

/-- A sieve containing every arrow whose source satisfies `P` is covering, if the arrows with
`P`-source generate a covering sieve of every object. -/
private theorem mem_of_forall_source {P : C → Prop}
    (hcov : ∀ W : C, Sieve.generate (fun (Z : C) (_ : Z ⟶ W) ↦ P Z) ∈ J W) {W : C} (S : Sieve W)
    (h : ∀ (T : C) (k : T ⟶ W), P T → S k) : S ∈ J W :=
  J.superset_covering ((Sieve.generate_le_iff _ _).2 fun T k hk ↦ h T k hk) (hcov W)

/-- **Injectivity on a sieve-generating family makes a morphism of sheaves of modules locally
injective.**  If every object of `C` has a covering sieve generated by arrows whose sources
satisfy `P`, and `f` is injective on the sections over every object satisfying `P`, then the
equalizer sieve of any two sections identified by `f` is covering. -/
theorem isLocallyInjective_val_of_injective_on {M N : SheafOfModules.{v} R} (f : M ⟶ N)
    (P : C → Prop)
    (hcov : ∀ W : C, Sieve.generate (fun (Z : C) (_ : Z ⟶ W) ↦ P Z) ∈ J W)
    (hinj : ∀ Z : C, P Z → Function.Injective (f.val.app (op Z))) :
    PresheafOfModules.IsLocallyInjective J f.val where
  equalizerSieve_mem {W} x y h :=
    mem_of_forall_source hcov _ fun T k hk ↦ show M.val.map k.op x = M.val.map k.op y from
      hinj T hk (by
        rw [PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply f.val k.op x,
          PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply f.val k.op y]
        exact congrArg (N.val.map k.op) h)

/-- **Surjectivity on a sieve-generating family makes a morphism of sheaves of modules locally
surjective.**  If every object of `C` has a covering sieve generated by arrows whose sources
satisfy `P`, and `f` is surjective on the sections over every object satisfying `P`, then the
image sieve of any section is covering. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_val_of_surjective_on {M N : SheafOfModules.{v} R} (f : M ⟶ N)
    (P : C → Prop)
    (hcov : ∀ W : C, Sieve.generate (fun (Z : C) (_ : Z ⟶ W) ↦ P Z) ∈ J W)
    (hsurj : ∀ Z : C, P Z → Function.Surjective (f.val.app (op Z))) :
    PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective J f.val where
  imageSieve_mem {W} s :=
    mem_of_forall_source hcov _ fun T k hk ↦ by
      obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hsurj T hk (N.val.map k.op s)
      exact ⟨t, ht⟩

/-- **A morphism of sheaves of modules which is bijective on the sections over the objects of a
sieve-generating family is an isomorphism.**

The family is given by a predicate `P` on the objects of the site such that the arrows with
`P`-source generate a covering sieve of every object. -/
theorem isIso_of_bijective_val_app_on {M N : SheafOfModules.{v} R} (f : M ⟶ N)
    (P : C → Prop)
    (hcov : ∀ W : C, Sieve.generate (fun (Z : C) (_ : Z ⟶ W) ↦ P Z) ∈ J W)
    (hb : ∀ Z : C, P Z → Function.Bijective (f.val.app (op Z))) :
    IsIso f :=
  have := isLocallyInjective_val_of_injective_on f P hcov fun Z hZ ↦ (hb Z hZ).1
  have := isLocallySurjective_val_of_surjective_on f P hcov fun Z hZ ↦ (hb Z hZ).2
  isIso_of_isLocallyBijective f

/-- The isomorphism of sheaves of modules determined by bijectivity on the sections over the
objects of a sieve-generating family. -/
noncomputable def isoOfBijectiveValAppOn {M N : SheafOfModules.{v} R} (f : M ⟶ N)
    (P : C → Prop)
    (hcov : ∀ W : C, Sieve.generate (fun (Z : C) (_ : Z ⟶ W) ↦ P Z) ∈ J W)
    (hb : ∀ Z : C, P Z → Function.Bijective (f.val.app (op Z))) :
    M ≅ N :=
  have := isIso_of_bijective_val_app_on f P hcov hb
  asIso f

/-- The forward morphism of `isoOfBijectiveValAppOn f P hcov hb` is `f`. -/
@[simp]
lemma isoOfBijectiveValAppOn_hom {M N : SheafOfModules.{v} R} (f : M ⟶ N) (P : C → Prop)
    (hcov : ∀ W : C, Sieve.generate (fun (Z : C) (_ : Z ⟶ W) ↦ P Z) ∈ J W)
    (hb : ∀ Z : C, P Z → Function.Bijective (f.val.app (op Z))) :
    (isoOfBijectiveValAppOn f P hcov hb).hom = f :=
  rfl

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
